WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.384 --> 00:00:03.840
- These ships show port calls
at ukraine's black sea ports

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.690
in the days before russia
invaded the country.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.800
Here's how that compares

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.589
to the days after the
fighting broke out six months

00:00:10.589 --> 00:00:12.000
after the war started

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.190
under the black sea grain
initiative, and then

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.640
again this summer after the
black sea grain deal fell apart.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.440
They show how moscow's economic war

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.700
against ukraine is playing out

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.430
in the black sea, causing
key Ukrainian exports

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.770
to plunge, something russia has benefited

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.950
from as its exports are
reaching record highs.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.500
So how has russia sought
to control shipping

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.670
to and from ukraine?

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.470
And what are kyiv and its allies trying

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.562
to do to counter that blockade?

00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:41.190
Before the war, ukraine's
black sea ports exported 95%

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.340
of the country's wheat,
corn, and sunflower oil.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.230
Ukraine's agricultural products account

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.170
for 41% of the country's total exports,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.930
meaning they are major
drivers of ukraine's economy.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.180
Wanting to choke ukraine off financially,

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.290
russia has taken aim

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.527
at these ports since the invasion began.

00:00:57.527 --> 00:00:59.880
It's done this in a
number of different ways.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.460
It's tried to capture
some strategic port cities

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.920
and it's bombarded others with missiles.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.860
It's also destroyed infrastructure
used to export grain

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.440
and moved warships into
shipping corridors.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.270
Now, there has been a caveat.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.020
Last July in turkey, moscow
under diplomatic pressure agreed

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.440
to a UN broker deal known as
the black sea grain initiative,

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.570
that paved the way for
ukrainian food products

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.780
and only food products to
flow from these three ports.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.490
You can see that port calls picked up

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.469
but they never fully recovered
to those pre-war levels

00:01:29.469 --> 00:01:32.220
and russia was accused
of slowing down shipping

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.140
by holding up inspections.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.080
Then this summer, shipping
came to a standstill once again

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.690
after russia withdrew from
that black sea grain deal

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.679
and threatened all commercial
ships heading toward ukraine.

00:01:42.679 --> 00:01:44.820
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.220
- So how are kyiv and its allies racing

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.600
to keep ukraine's economy

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.400
and its critical food products plugged

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.750
into the rest of the world?

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:52.590
Early in the war,

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.200
the European Union established
these solidarity lanes

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.460
to move products in and out

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.090
of the country via road,
rail, and inland waterways.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.820
Over much of the past year,
those overland routes handled

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.610
about 24% of ukraine's grain exports,

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.096
while the black sea ports handled 50%.

00:02:08.096 --> 00:02:10.470
Ports over here on the Danube River

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:12.630
handled the remaining 26%.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.910
Now following the collapse
of that grain deal,

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.490
the US is leading an
effort to increase capacity

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.430
here where grain is shipped
down the Danube River

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.130
and through romania's
ports on the black sea.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.630
Even though this route is slower

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.210
and more expensive than using
ukraine's black sea ports,

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.560
it's considered to be safer

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.320
since it lies under the nato umbrella.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.153
Ships would travel

00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:35.340
through the waters of
romania, bulgaria, and turkey.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.330
Those countries are part

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.240
of nato whose 31 members
consider an attack

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.700
on one to be an attack on all.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.850
Now, the UN and turkey are
still trying to get russia back

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.520
into that grain deal, but
that might not happen.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.340
So ukraine is also working
to open a shipping corridor

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.230
in the black sea, that would allow ships

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.120
to hug ukraine's coast before sailing

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.560
by those nato countries.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.170
That could help Ukrainian
farmers earn more money.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.990
But ukraine's ability to
resume exports this way depends

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.970
on whether ships can get insurance and

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.130
whether captains are
willing to take the risk

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.576
because russia isn't
guaranteeing them safe passage.

00:03:08.576 --> 00:03:10.110
The true test for ukraine

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:12.600
and its allies will come
in September and October

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.210
when the country's massive
harvests are brought in.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.164
But some ukrainian
farmers have already given

00:03:17.164 --> 00:03:18.990
up on planting their crops

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.480
since the market and
supply chain are broken

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.780
and there are no signs of
the war ending anytime soon.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.120
Now, as russia threatens these new routes,

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.240
the US says it's considering
all possible options

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.070
including military solutions

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:34.612
to protect the ships
heading to these ports.

00:03:34.612 --> 00:03:37.710
And analysts say the threat
of a broader war spilling

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.150
into the black sea is higher

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.836
than at any point since
the conflict began.

00:03:41.836 --> 00:03:44.336
(warm music)

